1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,760
If I wanted to go from white belt to blue belt as fast as I possibly could,

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:04,960
he's exactly what I would do.

3
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:07,200
I changed gyms and telomells already at blue belt.

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,880
No, please don't fucking do that.

5
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:10,000
I've heard of people doing that.

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,080
It's a very bad idea.

7
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:14,000
What I would actually do is in the first three months of my training,

8
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,360
I would heavily prioritize bottom position escapes.

9
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:21,080
Now that means things like north south side control, mount, half guard,

10
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:22,920
and you could even include the back in this one.

11
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:27,080
The bulk of your training in the first three months is going to be defending

12
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:29,280
and surviving in these positions.

13
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:33,440
If you want to speed that up, select two escapes from each of those positions

14
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:36,480
and make sure that you use them in conjunction with each other,

15
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:39,520
not just as random pieces you throw and hope work.

16
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:42,920
The next biggest problem that you need to solve that you're going to face

17
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:46,760
in your training as a white belt is actually starting to use offense

18
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,240
off the back of those escapes.

19
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:50,200
So many times I get asked the question,

20
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:52,920
oh, well, I escaped, so I controlled there to spin to north south.

21
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:53,760
What should I do?

22
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:57,720
We should start to fire off things like wrestling up or submission threats

23
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:01,800
so that you can actually stop your partner from just moving forwards

24
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:05,360
and get them to consider that you might be offering some sort of danger

25
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:08,040
and give you an opportunity to then turn the tide.

26
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:09,840
Once you turn the tide with offense,

27
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:12,960
you now need to reverse engineer all the things that you learn in the

28
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:17,200
pin escapes phase to start to pin your opponent on the floor.

29
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:21,040
It's all well and good if you can sweep them and threaten them with submissions

30
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:21,920
or wrestle up.

31
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:24,720
But if you can't keep them there, you've wasted your time.

32
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:29,320
Then and only then do you have the permission to focus on submissions

33
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:31,280
because if you can't escape from bottom position,

34
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:33,840
you can't generate offense, you can't pin your training partner.

35
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:36,920
The amount of subs that you're going to get is very limited anyway.

36
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,640
Position always precedes submission.

37
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:43,040
And until you learn that, you're not going to be getting many of them.

38
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:45,840
And the ones that you do get are going to be hail Mary's.

39
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:50,320
And if you want to be doing the sport for a long time to a high degree of quality,

40
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,040
you don't want to rely on hail Mary's.

41
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:53,880
And after you've pinned your training partner,

42
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:57,760
then you can start to isolate limbs and cruise to a submission finish.

43
00:01:57,760 --> 00:02:01,600
If you can do all that reliably to a variety of training partners,

44
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:04,400
as a white belt, I dare say you're very close to a blue belt.

